/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  liquidDensity06_NaClwaterEthanol -- D5 of the liquid-density pilot
  (C378): 30 water + 5 ethanol + 1 NaCl (kmol ratio), 298.15 K, 1 bar.  No
  solution record covers {ethanol, NaCl, water} and NaCl has no liquid
  volume, so the pump, the CSTR and the props bench (`rho_liquid_kernel`)
  REFUSE, naming the three constituents, the kind of record missing
  (parameters/solution/ethanol-NaCl-water.dat, a `liquidDensity` law for
  exactly these constituents) and the remedies.  The data that would fill
  it exist: Galleguillos, Taboada and Graber, J. Chem. Eng. Data 48 (2003)
  405-410 (21 saturated and 53 unsaturated points at 298.15 and 313.15 K).
  Before the pilot the pump ANSWERED here, leaving NaCl's volume out, 1.8 to
  4.1 % off the data.  `.expect-nonconvergence`: the refusal is the lesson,
  asserted by check_density_pilot.

  The flowsheet of every liquid-density demonstration: feed (1 kg/s) ->
  pump P1 (dP 2 bar, eta 0.7) -> CSTR R1 (V_R 1 m3, the reaction's reactant
  absent, see constant/reactions) -> product.  By hand, with rho the
  property kernel's liquid density printed in the run's table:
      Q   = m_dot / rho                 (the pump's volumetric flow)
      W   = Q dP / eta                  (its shaft power)
      h   = dP / (rho g)                (its head)
      tau = V_R rho / m_dot             (the CSTR's residence time, at its
                                         feed, the pump's outlet state)
  The pump prices its INLET state, the CSTR its FEED (the pump's outlet).
  Theory Guide: sec:liquid-density-methods.  Gate: check_density_pilot.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        P1;
        type        pump;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( pumped );
        operation   { dP 2 bar; eta 0.7; }
    }
    {
        name        R1;
        type        cstr;
        in          pumped;
        outputs     ( product );
        operation   { V_R 1; }
        reactions   ( absentAcid );
    }
);
